{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>The wife of the deceased I have acquired.</b> The meaning of this word is 'acquisition,' and a past-tense verb in place of future. For the wife has a ketubah, and the mother too inherits what remains. And it is written קניתי, and the meaning is 'so I will acquire.'"], :book :ruth, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ruth -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ruth"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:31.830410323Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}